      "data": {
        "text": "**Selecting OCR Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Vision AI for the OCR implementation. Now, the main thrust is ensuring that Google Cloud Vision AI is correctly and clearly identifiable as the chosen OCR provider within the `extract_text.py` file. I need to be explicit about this.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation Steps**\n\nI've sketched out the initial steps for `extract_text.py`. I'm starting by establishing that I will use the `google-cloud-vision` library. This involves importing `vision` from `google.cloud`.  I'll define a function, `extract_text_from_image`, that takes an image path. Within it, I'll initialize the Vision API client, handle the image loading and encoding to bytes (which the API requires), and then use the API's `text_detection` method. Finally, I'll focus on returning the extracted text.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789862793767,
          "start": 1789862790949
